{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795430360,"nonce":"Fx3DwINsTNFFTD5mINg/UNi0teU=","title":"Eight animation_paths tests fail at BLINC_ANIM_PATHS_SCALE=2 on a clean HEAD","message":"`BLINC_ANIM_PATHS_SCALE=2 cargo nextest run -p blinc_recorder --features headless --test animation_paths --run-ignored all --no-fail-fast` on 57a32d64 with nothing else applied (checked by stashing the add9f78 work): 31 pass, 8 fail. At the default density all 39 pass, which is what CI runs.\n\nFailing:\n- a_label_turns_with_its_card\n- a_css_animated_label_follows_its_card_on_rows\n- a_css_transitioned_label_follows_its_card_on_rows\n- a_css_fade_of_a_single_primitive_rides_rows_and_shows\n- text_scaled_by_a_css_animation_is_sharp_while_it_plays\n- text_zoomed_by_a_spring_is_sharp_while_it_moves\n- the_scrollbar_of_a_container_on_rows_is_drawn_and_follows_the_scroll\n- the_node_table_beside_other_bindings\n\nAt least one is the test, not the renderer: `the_scrollbar_of_a_container_on_rows_is_drawn_and_follows_the_scroll` samples the track at `pixel(frame, W - 7, y)` for `y in 0..H`, which are logical sizes, so at 2x it reads a column in the middle of the frame and the top half only. The new `a_fading_scrollbar_over_still_content_takes_the_fast_path` takes the density from `frame.width / W` and passes at both densities. The others have not been read yet: each needs a look at whether it measures in logical pixels against a physical frame, or whether the rows path really differs at 2x, which is the density of every Mac window.","files":null}]}